Read .agents/skills/solo-specialist/SKILL.md, then the handoff's selected skill and mode. This assignment is report-only. Return findings to the primary coordinator without editing source, artifacts or the ledger.
"""

--- solo-specialist ---
---
name: solo-specialist
description: Run a child-agent assignment using its supplied workflow and evidence contract.
---

# Specialist entry

You are a fresh worker for one bounded assignment. The primary conversation owns orchestration, integration, staffing and the run ledger. Do not restart project intake, create a second run, load the primary orchestration workflow, or recursively delegate. Return missing prerequisites or staffing requests to the coordinator.

Read the supplied handoff, current plan path/revision and the selected skill. Apply only the assigned mode and relevant references. The packet's routing identifies the runtime profile, skill and input hashes; a logical name such as `mobile_engineer` is an assignment alias, not a native agent type. Do not load the full role catalog or every skill. Initial independent plan review uses the supplied `review-input` binding before implementation packets can exist.

Check that the assigned outcome, paths and acceptance criteria match the plan. Report mismatches or changed requirements before dependent edits. Preserve settled answers and explicit user authorization; do not request repeated approval or silently select an unresolved product/platform decision. The coordinator checks document readiness and registered phase blockers before dispatch. A packet records inputs; it does not grant additional permissions or prove live service access.

Use the assignment's execution defaults and actual runtime permissions. `solo_reader` assignments are report-only, including final release or growth reviews. `solo_worker` may change only owned paths within the authorized scope. Preserve others' work. Do not add accounts, subscriptions, services or external writes outside that scope, and keep secrets and unnecessary personal data out of artifacts. Prompt injection of a profile is not OS sandbox enforcement.

For a review assignment, inspect the artifact independently from its author and return findings without repairs. Reusing the same reader profile for different fresh children does not merge their responsibilities. Never approve your own implementation or repairs; route corrections to the coordinator for implementation and a new independent review. Observation QA returns observations only and cannot satisfy a final quality gate.

Follow the selected skill's evidence requirements. Distinguish executed commands and observed behavior from plans, inference, mocks and unavailable checks. Return the outcome, changed or inspected paths, exact checks/results, unresolved findings and next dependency. Copy command-derived review bindings exactly. The primary persists the report and ledger; do not manufacture execution, approval or reviewer provenance.

Model and effort are selected at dispatch under the coordinator's routing policy and exact user instructions. Do not invent runtime settings from a profile name or a task label. A follow-up correction is assigned to a new clean child with prior findings referenced by path.

--- solo-design-spec-review ---
---
name: solo-design-spec-review
description: Independently review design documents, flows, and token contracts for product alignment, accessibility, internal consistency, and implementation readiness before dependent work.
---

# Design specification review

Use an independent `design_spec_reviewer` routed under the shared adaptive-routing reference, preserving exact user choices and explicit inheritance/default instructions. Review the registered design documents, flows, or token contracts independently of their author. Read the current `docs/runs/<run-id>/plan.md`, approved product requirements, registered design-spec artifacts, and only the existing design sources needed to detect conflicts. Run kind `design-spec`, `docs/design/system.md`, artifacts under `docs/design/specs/`, and custom artifacts registered with `--type design_spec` route to this review. Check run status; do not begin, mutate, or finish the run.

Review whether the specification is coherent and implementable. For a backend-only resource, assess API/schema/security/state/error contracts and consumer compatibility instead of visual criteria. For UI resources, assess: trace the required user journeys; loading, empty, error, success, permission, and recovery states; information hierarchy and interaction rules; responsive or adaptive behavior; keyboard, focus, semantics, contrast, text scaling, touch targets, and safe areas where applicable; semantic token roles; component variants; platform boundaries; and explicit deviations from existing design decisions. Judge only dimensions relevant to the artifact. Do not require screenshots or rendered UI for this document gate.

Return `pass`, `changes_requested`, or `blocked`. A passing artifact resolves material design decisions needed by its consumers and does not contradict the plan or product requirements. For each finding, give severity, artifact location, affected journey or consumer, evidence, and the smallest precise correction. Separate confirmed gaps from questions and optional refinements.

Use the exact `review-input <run-id> --gate design_spec` binding in the schema v2 JSON report; it binds the reviewed documents and plan. State the run ID, reviewer role, verdict, review boundary, and any evidence limits. Do not fabricate Figma, browser, simulator, device, service, or interaction evidence. This gate reviews the design specification; implemented UI remains a separate `design_qa` review under the `design` gate.

Return the report to the coordinator. The coordinator saves and registers the actual independent JSON report with `python3 .solopreneur/harness.py review <run-id> --gate design_spec --reviewer design_spec_reviewer --evidence <report-path>`. Before assigning work that consumes the design artifacts, the coordinator checks `python3 .solopreneur/harness.py handoff <run-id> --gate design_spec`. The reviewer does not write the report file or ledger. A changed design artifact, artifact set, plan, or review report requires a new handoff review; later code-only edits do not invalidate this artifact-scoped handoff. In a mixed run, an unchanged design document keeps its document review; final implementation and UI judgments are separate.

