"affected\_journey\_or\_consumer": "Host session removal after a fork, especially after an UNKNOWN\_OUTCOME fork",  
"evidence": "The contract refuses only sessions with registered descendants. A timed-out session.fork can have created an SDK child without returning enough information for the app to register it. The installed 2.0.18 SDK exposes SessionInfo.parentID, session.list({ parentID, cursor, ... }) and a paginated SessionsResponse, so registered-app state alone cannot prove descendant absence. The same pagination issue applies if list membership is used to prove post-remove absence.",  
