"affected\_journey\_or\_consumer": "Duplicate fork/remove requests after transport timeout or other UNKNOWN\_OUTCOME",  
"evidence": "The contract says exact duplicates return a current safe snapshot, while also stating that unknown effects retain an unknown receipt, cannot be replayed, and must never imply an accepted fork/delete. Returning an ordinary successful snapshot for an exact duplicate whose stored receipt is unknown does not preserve that distinction and can make an uncertain destructive/history mutation appear successful.",  
"correction": "Define receipt-state-specific duplicate behavior: an exact duplicate of a known-success receipt may return the authoritative current snapshot; an exact duplicate of an UNKNOWN\_OUTCOME receipt must return the fixed UNKNOWN\_OUTCOME failure without replay until an explicitly specified deterministic reconciliation changes that receipt state. Conflicting fingerprints remain DUPLICATE\_CONFLICT."  
}  
\],  
